A||||11||Alex4mula||Interior paint. Help on procedure.||||1||
Z||000000||Alex4mula||03-14-2001||12:21 PM||||I have my gray interior paint. Auto paint shop mixed a PPG formula for interior parts.<BR>Do I need a spray gun for this? Could I get by with the small air-gun kit that Radio Shacks sell for hobbyist?<BR>I'm planning on doing only the door's arm rest and bottom door plastic trim.<BR>Can I use just acetone to clean the parts before painting? Or do I need a special chemical?<BR>Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||03-14-2001||04:26 PM||||???||||reg||1
Z||000002||Loki||03-14-2001||04:35 PM||||Just go to say Wal-Mart and buy some vinyl cleaner and clean it good let dry and paint....Also, I just used plain ol' vinyl paint from an auto store...like 2 somethng a can....Already has spray thing   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> works wonders and matched perfectly<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||GoCartGuy||03-14-2001||05:48 PM||||Alex,<P>First off, use acetone to clean the vinyl...a typical vinyl cleaner leaves a residue, not good for paint adhesion.  Second, you said you had a PPG formula mixed, what kind of paint base?  Your best bet is a latex for flexability.  Whether or not you can spray it depends on which paint you're using and the spray gun.  Most sprayers can't handle a good latex.<BR>Just the 2 cents from a paint guy at Lowe's, who's also working on his interior.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000004||Loki||03-14-2001||06:18 PM||||Unsure what vinyl cleaner your usung but what I use (tuff stuff) it works wonders and has no residue and the paint sticks damn good.....Just to let ya know   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex4mula||03-14-2001||06:33 PM||||The paint says "Elastomeric Color System". If I can't use spray gun, what do I use? A brush? I haven't opened the can but it feels very very thin.||||reg||1
Z||000006||GoCartGuy||03-14-2001||07:42 PM||||Alex,<P>An elastomeric is a latex based.  First check the paperwork with the sprayer you're looking at.  If it says "no" to latex, skip it, even if it does feel thin.  If it says it'll handle some latex you can give it a shot if you want.  If you get globs or uneven spraying, the paints probably too thick.  Either way, I'd check with the guy who mixed it for you and see what he recomends, or you can ask FieroLisa, she just repainted her interior with a spray gun assembly.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||03-14-2001||08:41 PM||||its already pre thinned to be ready to spray. yes you can use an airbrush or even a small touch up spray gun. Clean thoughly with acetone, then go back over it with alcohol, use a brush to get into the vinyl grain. Keep wiping and drying with paper towels. Ask fierolisa for the whole thing-she just did her interior from tan to gray. Bad part was someone had used armor all everywhere, and paint dont get along with it at all, everywhere she didnt get good n clean wants to scratch pretty ez.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex4mula||03-14-2001||09:20 PM||||Good. Thanks a lot guys.||||reg||1
Z||000009||GoCartGuy||03-20-2001||10:40 AM||||Alex,<P>Got two questions for ya.  First off, what's the brand name of the paint you're using? Second, did you decide on what sprayer to use?  If so, which one did you go with?<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroLisa||03-20-2001||01:06 PM||||definitely definitely clean the parts well!!! Use acetone- I did the whole interior and everything is sticking well except my driver side armrest- the worst place to not clean well! I'm gonna have to do a crappy touch up job until i can get home and use the spray gun and re paint it.<BR>anyway if you have any other questions, email me, since i just got done doing the whole dang thing.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT- 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air,<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Alex4mula||03-20-2001||08:51 PM||||I ended up using a can sprayer sold in Home Depot. Very cheap, less than $4 and comes with a crystal bottle to pour the paint. Spray refills are like $3 bucks also. I cleaned the parts very well with acetone, alcohol and finaly water. Sprayer do not has the best spray characeristics but did the job very well. Results were excellent. I did the arm rest and bottom plastic trim. If interested you may see it in Daytona. Thanks again for your input.||||reg||1
